{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md'","aggregated_output":"# 判断的尺子，第 1 版（D3 立场金标）\n\n写于 2026-11-02。Alex 的话：\"你已经改了好几次尺子了，到底什么是对的，以及你怎么 freeze。\"\n\n## 0. 一句话\n\n一道题判得对不对，拿它和**一位资深对冲基金分析师读完同样 14 天材料后的看法**比：他认为市场原来预期什么、材料推出来的结果是多少、\n相对预期是高是低；系统最后一次判断落的那一档，有没有把这个结果包进去。分析师不是我，不是写代码的人，不看系统的输出；他的看法写成文件、算出\nsha256、记进决定，之后一个字不改。\n\n## 1. 什么是\"对\"\n\n- **单位**：一道金标题 × 一个时点（14 天窗口末，2026-07-14 收盘后）。23 道题：22 道种子（`poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json` v1–v22，每次运行里\n  编号固定）加金标 must_open 里种子没覆盖的 1 道（俄亥俄租约担保是/否，2026-07-01 的 must_open）。其余 27 条 must_open 都是这 23 道的同一赌注\n  （信用支持金额 ×10、Kyber 出货 ×11、云厂商资本开支 ×5、内存价格 ×1、中国放行 H200 ×2），映射写在 `questions-v1.json` 里，Alex 签。\n- **材料**：签过的抽取标准对这 14 天的读法，即金标 golden-v5（dev，118 篇）的 309 条事项（核心 86、辅助 151、可选 72），带日期、标题、\n  来源层、说话人、原文和意思。不用系统的账本（账本随每臂变，尺子不能随臂变），不用原始全文（那是重做抽取）。这和抽取的尺子是同一把：标准第 5 节\n  说的\"分析员会记的\"就是这些。\n- **分析师写什么**（每道题一条，`reader-brief.md` 是他拿到的全部说明，里面只有标准和 PRD 06 的原话，没有系统的提示词）：\n  1. `reference`：到 2026-07-14 为止市场预期这道题的答案是什么（一致预期、公司指引、既定计划或截止日），出自哪几条事项；材料里没有就写\n     \"没有，参照 = 现状\"。\n  2. `implied_outcome`：材料推出来的结果——数字题给一个数或一个区间，事件题给是/否和日期——怎么推的，出自哪几条。\n  3. `direction`：结果相对参照：above / in_line / below；事件题 yes / no。\n  4. `confidence`：high / medium / low（材料把这件事定到什么程度）。\n  5. `decisive_items`：撑起这个看法的 2–6 条事项编号；`against`：最强的反面一条。\n  6. `no_view`：材料里没有任何关于这道题的东西时为 true；这道题不进分数，记\"没练到\"。\n  7. `reasoning`：三到六句。只用材料，不用材料外的知识，每个说法都要有编号。\n- **分析师是谁**：两位互相独立、都没写过这套代码也没看过系统输出的模型读者（A：Codex；B：一个干净上下文的 Claude 读者），各自从同一个包\n  写一遍。都标明\"模型写的\"。**Alex 定（2026-11-02，D262）：金标 = 读者 B 的 23 条答案，原样；读者 A 的答案留作对照记录**，两者的差别\n  （区间或是/否不同 3/23：q09、q12、q23；方向标签不同 12/20）就是这把尺子自身噪声的记录（`reconcile-v1.md`）。\n- **判\"对\"的方法**（`score_judgement.py`，全部是代码）：取一次运行里每道题在 2026-07-14 及之前最后一次判断。数字题：金标的区间\n  [low, high] 和系统所选那一档的 [lo, hi) 有没有交集，有 = 一致；事件题：是/否相同 = 一致。没判过的题单独数（那是证据没到，D2 的事，不算\n  判断错）。另外打印两条零假设：**查表基线**（把金标写的参照数落进哪一档，就选那一档）和**永远中性基线**；判断要在这两条线之上才算有判断力。\n  读者之间的分歧率一起打印，那是尺子自身的噪声。\n- **第二层，读不是数**：分数之外，对一个样本的判断，由没写代码的读者看系统写的理由（从 judging-v6 起还有 reference 和 implied_outcome）\n  是不是从所示证据得出。这是 AGENTS §7.2 的\"分数是线索、trace 是测量\"。\n\n## 2. 怎么 freeze\n\n原则先于机制（D261，Alex 2026-11-02：\"我们做完的 review 过的尺子金标不能再动了\"）：这一页、读者说明、题单和金标在 Alex 审过签字之后一个字不改；之前只在建的过程中改，签字前不拿它打任何分。下面是把这句话变成代码和文件的做法。\n\n1. 读者只看 `packet-v1.json` 和 `reader-brief.md`，看不到任何运行、账本、提示词；读者的原始答案 `reader-A.json`、`reader-B.json` 原样保存，不改。\n2. 我不写金标。我做的只有：拼包（代码）、按 direction 机械对齐两位读者、把分歧按材料写成对照记录（引编号）；分歧由材料定，定不了的列给 Alex。\n3. 金标文件 `gold-v1.json` 带 `ruler_version: 1`、两位读者的 sha256、每道题的来源（A/B 一致，或裁定及理由）；文件的 sha256 写进\n   `gold-v1.sha256` 和决定 D261。Alex 签的是：23 道题的清单和映射、裁定过的题。签之前每个分数都标\"金标第 1 版，未签\"。\n4. `score_judgement.py` 开头读金标的 sha256 和 `ruler_version`，和自己写死的对不上就拒绝打分，打印两边的 sha；每份分数都印金标版本。\n5. 冻住后不改文件。发现错了，写进 `corrections-v1.json` 一条带日期的记录：哪道题、改前、改后、为什么；打分器不悄悄应用它，只在分数旁印\n   \"有 N 条更正未并入\"。更正积累到要并入时，出第 2 版：新文件、新 sha、决定里记，旧分数作废并说明。\n6. 这一页的定义本身改了（单位、材料、字段、判对的方法），就是第 2 版尺子：金标必须重写，打分器拒绝版本不符的金标。改定义只能由记录在 Alex\n   原话上的决定触发（AGENTS §7.1）。\n7. 一把尺子：判断这一步不再有别的评分标准。我昨天定的判断规则 D260 是系统这边的规则，不是尺子；读者的说明里没有它。\n\n**冻结记录**：2026-11-02，`gold-v1.json` sha256 `636c056d1e4252fa759660803067e6ccd67a81067b012905e918aa9dec4005f2`，写在 `gold-v1.sha256` 和 `score_judgement.py` 里；`corrections-v1.json` 为空。当天下午提过的两条改法（读者分叉时打三档分；五五开的题不计分）Alex 没采纳：一题一个区间，每题都算。\n\n这把尺子作为整体（抽取标准 + 题目 + 判断）写在 AGENTS §7.1 \"The frozen ruler\"，每个文件的 sha256 由 `tests/test_frozen_rulers.py` 守着：任何一个动了，整套测试变红。\n\n## 2′. 这把尺子沿用了什么，新的只有哪一层\n\n沿用、不重做：抽取标准页（第 3 版签字 D243 + D250 的四条界线）和 golden-v5 是这把尺子的**材料**，按 sha 引用（`packet-v1.json` 记了金标的 sha）；golden-v5 的题目部分（28 条 must_open，题目标准第 3 版）映射进 23 道题；种子 v2（D253）给题的身份和档的边界；PRD 06 的判断规则和 AGENTS §8 的分析师原话是读者说明里的全部规则；桌面尺子 README 的 D1、D2 不动。2026-10-27 的步骤 3/4 金标（`research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/`，24 例，量的是重复 / 替换 / 并入的决定，不是档位）里写的分析师标准 A（谁先说的，复述只加一个出处不加事实）、B（期间和定义要对上，季度不是全年）和这份说明一致，两者量的是不同步骤；那份金标是在旧账本上写的，助手自己写的，当时就标了不是独立金标。新的只有一层：判断这一步的档位从来没有金标，这是第一份，还有打分器。\n\n## 3. 这把尺子不量什么\n\n该开的题开了没有（D1）、证据挂得对不对（D2）、14 天里每天的路径、依赖和主题推力。它只量：窗口末，系统的档位有没有包住分析师认为的结果。\n\n## 4. 已知的弱点，写明\n\n- 读者是模型，不是人。金标是一位读者（B）的看法，Alex 选的；另一位（A）留作对照，两者在 3/23 道题上区间不交，这是尺子的噪声下限；Alex 的裁定是人的那一票。\n- 材料外的知识：事后结果（FY2027 年报、2026 年底 Rubin 出不出货）都在模型知识截止之后，无法作弊；但模型可能用它记得的\"常识\"补材料，说明里\n  禁止并要求每句引编号，对照时查。\n- 参照：材料里不一定有每道题的一致预期（内存价格、CoWoS 产能），那时参照是现状，direction 的意义弱一点，分数仍按区间交集算。\n- 种子的档不是围着一致预期写的（总收入题一致预期 $392B 落在中性档 350–400 的上沿）：所以分数不比\"看涨/看跌\"的标签，只比区间有没有包住。\n\n## 5. 文件\n\n`judgement-gold/`：`ruler-v1.md`（本页）、`reader-brief.md`、`build_packet.py` → `packet-v1.json` + `questions-v1.json`、\n`run_reader_codex.py` → `reader-A.json`、读者 B 的答案 `reader-B.json`、`reconcile.py` → `gold-v1.json` + `reconcile-v1.md`、\n`gold-v1.sha256`、`corrections-v1.json`、`score_judgement.py`。\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/packet-figures-controls.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n \"statements\": [\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-04\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA generated $96.22 billion of second-quarter revenue and $63.73 billion of operating income, an operating margin of about 66%, according to the article.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"second quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"$96.22 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"company-reported quarterly revenue\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"operating margin\",\n     \"period\": \"second quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"about 66%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"derived from reported revenue and operating income\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S1\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's latest reported quarter generated $89 billion of data-center revenue out of $96.2 billion in total revenue, so roughly 92.5% of sales came from the infrastructure businesses powering large-scale AI, according to GuruFocus's recounting of the results in its 22 September 2026 article.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Data-center revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"latest reported quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"$89 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Data-center segment revenue, as reported in the company's quarterly results\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Total revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"latest reported quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"$96.2 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Company-wide revenue\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Data-center share of total sales\",\n     \"period\": \"latest reported quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"roughly 92.5%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Data-center revenue divided by total revenue, as calculated by GuruFocus\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 16,\n   \"ref\": \"S2\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's gross margin is guided to settle in the 72% to 73% range in fiscal 2028, lowered because memory prices have risen more than management expected, partly helped by price increases the company has already executed.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Gross margin\",\n     \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028\",\n     \"value\": \"72% to 73%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"Company gross margin guidance, lowered on higher-than-expected memory costs and helped by price increases already executed\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S3\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-28\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA said on Monday 28 September 2026 that it authorized an additional $150 billion for its share repurchase program, taking the total authorization to $235 billion, which it described as the largest increase in a share repurchase authorization in history; the company said it expects to complete the total remaining buyback program through fiscal 2028.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"additional share repurchase authorization\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"$150 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Additional authorization; takes total buyback authorization to $235 billion, expected to be completed through fiscal 2028.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"total share repurchase authorization\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"$235 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Total program after the additional $150 billion authorization.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 32,\n   \"ref\": \"S4\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-29\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA has a $150 billion share buyback plan, described by Yahoo Finance as the largest ever, which the article cites alongside its cash generation as justification for the repurchase programme.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"share buyback plan\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"$150 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"announced repurchase authorisation; described as the largest ever\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S5\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue growth of 85% year over year, with Data Center revenues up 92% year over year, as retold by Zacks Equity Research in its Analyst Blog highlights.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"revenue growth\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2027 first quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"85%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"year over year, company total\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Data Center revenues growth\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2027 first quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"92%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"year over year, Data Center segment\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 3,\n   \"ref\": \"S6\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-25\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA reset its gross margin expectations after memory prices rose more than it expected, guiding gross margin to 74% for fiscal Q3 2027, down from 75% in fiscal Q2 2027, and expecting gross margin to bottom at 71% to 72% in fiscal Q4 2027.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"gross margin\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q3 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"74%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"company guided, down from fiscal Q2 2027\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"gross margin\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q2 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"75%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"company\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"gross margin\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q4 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"71% to 72%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"expected bottom\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 6,\n   \"ref\": \"S7\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-27\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA says its $108 billion revenue forecast for the current quarter assumes no China data-center chip revenue; any China data-center chip sales would come on top of that outlook.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Revenue forecast for the current quarter\",\n     \"period\": \"Current quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"$108 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"Company forecast; assumes no China data-center chip revenue\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S8\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's second-quarter net income rose 126% year-on-year to $59.7bn, according to the Yahoo Finance UK article, which notes earnings grew roughly 4.5 times faster than the share price over the same comparison.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Net income\",\n     \"period\": \"Second quarter (year-on-year)\",\n     \"value\": \"$59.7bn\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Net income growth, year-on-year\",\n     \"period\": \"Second quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"126%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 3,\n   \"ref\": \"S9\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-01\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 EPS of $2.22, topping the $2.09 consensus and marking its fifth consecutive beat, according to the article.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Earnings per share\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$2.22\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"as reported\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Consensus earnings per share\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$2.09\",\n     \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n     \"basis\": \"consensus estimate\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S10\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-04\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia reported free cash flow of $27.02 billion in the fiscal year ended January 2024, $60.85 billion in fiscal 2025 and $96.68 billion in fiscal 2026.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"free cash flow\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal year ended January 2024\",\n     \"value\": \"$27.02 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"free cash flow\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal year ended January 2025\",\n     \"value\": \"$60.85 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"free cash flow\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal year ended January 2026\",\n     \"value\": \"$96.68 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S11\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-29\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's free cash flow fell by more than half in the quarter before the 29 September 2026 article, mostly because accounts receivable rose by more than $22 billion; the article states the sales were booked but the cash had not yet been collected.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"free cash flow\",\n     \"period\": \"last quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"fell by more than half\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"company change in free cash flow versus prior year quarter\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S12\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-25\",\n   \"statement\": \"Fool.com reports that Nvidia's sales to two direct customers represented 22% and 14% of total revenue, respectively, in fiscal 2026, and that two customers make up more than a third of sales — a customer concentration it flags as a risk.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Sales to a direct customer as % of total revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2026 (ended January 2026)\",\n     \"value\": \"22%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"direct customer\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Sales to a direct customer as % of total revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2026 (ended January 2026)\",\n     \"value\": \"14%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"direct customer\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 3,\n   \"ref\": \"S13\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia, in its quarterly results reported in the month before this 23 September 2026 Barchart article, posted what the article calls a market-beating fiscal Q2 and issued guidance for about 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"revenue growth\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2028\",\n     \"value\": \"about 70%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"Nvidia's own guidance as reported by Barchart; growth measure not further specified in the item\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 17,\n   \"ref\": \"S14\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-02\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA management's gross margin outlook remains at 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points, according to Insider Monkey; the item gives no period or statement date for the outlook, and the author adds that holding that margin requires absorbing rising high-bandwidth memory costs and higher R&D spending.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"gross margin outlook\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"74%, plus or minus 50 basis points\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"management outlook as reported by the article; item does not state the period covered\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S15\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-01\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA generated $24.08 billion in operating cash flow and $21.34 billion in free cash flow during fiscal Q2 2027.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Operating cash flow\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 fiscal 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$24.08 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Free cash flow\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 fiscal 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$21.34 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S16\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA management guided fiscal third-quarter revenue to approximately $108 billion, which the article says implies 89% growth.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Revenue guidance\",\n     \"period\": \"Fiscal third quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"approximately $108 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"Company guidance; implied 89% growth is the article's calculation\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 30,\n   \"ref\": \"S17\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia told shareholders in May 2026 that it would raise its quarterly dividend to $0.25 per share from $0.01 per share, an increase the Morningstar author calculates at 2,400%. The author estimates roughly $25 billion per year would be returned to shareholders through the dividend, which would make Nvidia one of the largest dividend payers in the US market; that annual figure is the author's approximation, not a company-disclosed total.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"quarterly dividend per share\",\n     \"period\": \"from the May 2026 declaration\",\n     \"value\": \"$0.25 per share\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"quarterly payout, raised from $0.01 per share\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"prior quarterly dividend per share\",\n     \"period\": \"prior to the May 2026 declaration\",\n     \"value\": \"$0.01 per share\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"increase in quarterly dividend\",\n     \"period\": \"May 2026 declaration\",\n     \"value\": \"2,400%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"author's calculation\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"annual dividend paid to shareholders\",\n     \"period\": \"annual, based on the May 2026 rate\",\n     \"value\": \"$25 billion per year\",\n     \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n     \"basis\": \"author's approximation (\\\"Something like\\\"); total annual dividend return to shareholders\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S18\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n   \"statement\": \"Broadcom AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion in Q2, up 143% year over year.\",\n   \"figures\": [],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S19\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-29\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia reported free cash flow of $69.9 billion for the first half of fiscal 2027, 77% higher than a year before, or around $35 billion a quarter; CEO Jensen Huang linked the buyback increase to the company's \\\"cash generation\\\" in the announcement.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"free cash flow\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2027 first half\",\n     \"value\": \"$69.9 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"company reported; around $35 billion a quarter\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"free cash flow growth\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2027 first half vs a year before\",\n     \"value\": \"77%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"higher than a year before\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S20\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-28\",\n   \"statement\": \"Former Wall Street analyst David Bennett, writing on X.com and quoted by the article, stated that Nvidia generated $74.4 billion of operating cash flow in the first half of fiscal year 2027 alone while still returning $46.1 billion to shareholders, which he said lets the company fund AI expansion and buy back stock at the same time.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"operating cash flow\",\n     \"period\": \"first half of fiscal year 2027 (through July 2026)\",\n     \"value\": \"$74.4 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"operating cash flow, company level\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S21\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's revenue more than doubled year over year in fiscal Q2 2027.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Revenue, year-over-year change\",\n     \"period\": \"Fiscal Q2 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"more than doubled\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Company-level, year over year\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 38,\n   \"ref\": \"S22\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-25\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's board approved raising the quarterly dividend from $0.01 to $0.25 per share in May 2026, a 2,400% increase that lifted the quarterly payout from about $243 million (fiscal 2027 first quarter, when the penny dividend was still in force) to approximately $6.0 billion. The first $0.25 payment went out on 26 June 2026 to holders of record as of 4 June, and a second $0.25 distribution went ex-dividend on 10 September 2026 with payment scheduled for 1 October 2026; the new annual rate is $1 per share.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"quarterly dividend per share\",\n     \"period\": \"quarterly, from May 2026\",\n     \"value\": \"$0.25 per share\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"raised from $0.01 per share per quarter; board-approved in May\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"quarterly dividend payout, total\",\n     \"period\": \"per quarter after the increase\",\n     \"value\": \"approximately $6.0 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"approximate, based on company disclosures and share counts at the time of payment\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"quarterly dividend cash outlay\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2027 first quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"about $243 million\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"at the prior $0.01 per share quarterly rate\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S23\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-05\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA spent $20 billion on share repurchases in its most recent quarter and $40 billion in the first half of fiscal 2027, split evenly at $20 billion in each of the first and second quarters, according to the article.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"share repurchases (buybacks)\",\n     \"period\": \"most recent quarter (Q2 fiscal 2027)\",\n     \"value\": \"$20 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"company-wide buyback spend\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"share repurchases (buybacks)\",\n     \"period\": \"first half of fiscal 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$40 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"$20 billion in each of the first and second quarters\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S24\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-29\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia's diluted share count for its fiscal 2027 second quarter, which ended July 26, 2026, was only about 1% smaller than a year before despite almost $40 billion of buybacks in the fiscal year's first half; earnings per share more than doubled.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"earnings per share growth\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2027 second quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"more than doubled\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S25\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-28\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA said its revenue opportunity per gigawatt of AI infrastructure, based on its reference designs, has risen from roughly $18 billion during the Hopper generation to $25 billion with Blackwell and $40 billion with Rubin.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Revenue opportunity per gigawatt of AI infrastructure (Hopper generation)\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"roughly $18 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n     \"basis\": \"NVIDIA's estimate based on its reference designs; per gigawatt of AI infrastructure\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Revenue opportunity per gigawatt of AI infrastructure (Blackwell generation)\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"$25 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n     \"basis\": \"NVIDIA's estimate based on its reference designs; per gigawatt of AI infrastructure\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Revenue opportunity per gigawatt of AI infrastructure (Rubin generation)\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"$40 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n     \"basis\": \"NVIDIA's estimate based on its reference designs; per gigawatt of AI infrastructure\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 5,\n   \"ref\": \"S26\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-04\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA says Grace Blackwell is already one generation behind Vera Rubin and that Vera Rubin delivers 35 times lower token costs than Grace Blackwell Ultra; NVIDIA estimates about $25 billion of revenue per gigawatt for Grace Blackwell and roughly $40 billion per gigawatt for Vera Rubin.\",\n   \"figures\": [],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S27\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-29\",\n   \"statement\": \"In NVIDIA's fiscal Q2 2027, sales to the largest cloud companies were $49 billion, up 13% from the prior quarter, while sales to all other data center customers were $40 billion, up 25% from the prior quarter.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"sales to the largest cloud companies\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q2 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$49 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"largest cloud company customers only\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"sales to the largest cloud companies, change from prior quarter\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q2 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"13%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"quarter over quarter\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"sales to all other data center customers\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q2 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$40 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"data center customers other than the largest cloud companies\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"sales to all other data center customers, change from prior quarter\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q2 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"25%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"quarter over quarter\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 3,\n   \"ref\": \"S28\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-28\",\n   \"statement\": \"Trefis reports that NVIDIA's operating margin — the share of revenue left after running costs — is 65%, the highest in ten years, versus a three-year average of 59% (the article does not state the exact measurement period).\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"operating margin\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"65%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"share of revenue left after running costs; highest in ten years\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"operating margin (three-year average)\",\n     \"period\": \"three-year average\",\n     \"value\": \"59%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"three-year average\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S29\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-27\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA has already set price increases that take effect in fiscal Q1 2028, and management expects the higher prices to lift gross margin to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Gross margin\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2028\",\n     \"value\": \"72% to 73%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"management expectation, helped by price increases taking effect in fiscal Q1 2028\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S30\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-27\",\n   \"statement\": \"The low end of NVIDIA management's gross margin guidance for fiscal Q3 2027 is 73.5%, per the article.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Gross margin guidance, low end\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q3 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"73.5%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"low end of management's gross margin guide for the quarter\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S31\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n   \"statement\": \"fool.com reports that NVIDIA generated $192.9 billion in net income over the trailing 12 months, compared with $6.4 billion for AMD, citing this in a valuation comparison of the two AI chip makers.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"net income\",\n     \"period\": \"trailing 12 months\",\n     \"value\": \"$192.9 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S32\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-25\",\n   \"statement\": \"Fool.com reports that Nvidia's fiscal 2026, which ended in January 2026, produced revenue of nearly $215.9 billion, up roughly 65.5% year over year, net income of approximately $120.1 billion, and a net margin of approximately 55.6%, consistent with the 55.8% net margin of the previous fiscal year.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2026 (ended January 2026)\",\n     \"value\": \"$215.9 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"company total; up roughly 65.5% year over year\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Net income\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2026 (ended January 2026)\",\n     \"value\": \"$120.1 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"company total\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Net margin\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2026 (ended January 2026)\",\n     \"value\": \"55.6%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"company net margin; prior fiscal year 55.8%\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 6,\n   \"ref\": \"S33\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-02\",\n   \"statement\": \"In its latest reported quarter, Nvidia spent $19.7 billion on share buybacks and $6 billion on dividends, versus Apple's $25.9 billion of buybacks and $4 billion of dividends in Apple's fiscal 2026 third quarter; a year earlier, in the second quarter of Nvidia's fiscal 2026, Nvidia's buybacks and dividends combined totaled $10 billion.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"share buybacks\",\n     \"period\": \"latest reported quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"$19.7 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Nvidia share repurchases\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"dividends paid\",\n     \"period\": \"latest reported quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"$6 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Nvidia dividends\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"buybacks and dividends combined\",\n     \"period\": \"second quarter of fiscal 2026 (year-ago quarter)\",\n     \"value\": \"$10 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Nvidia share repurchases plus dividends, combined\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S34\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-27\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA management expects Vera Rubin to account for about 20% of data center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Vera Rubin share of data center revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q3 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"about 20%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"management expectation; share of data center revenue\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 5,\n   \"ref\": \"S35\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-12\",\n   \"statement\": \"Broadcom plans to ramp production of custom AI chips for Meta Platforms, Anthropic, and OpenAI from late 2026 into 2027.\",\n   \"figures\": [],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S36\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-01\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA returned approximately $25.78 billion through share repurchases and dividends in fiscal Q2 2027, and in late September 2026 increased its share repurchase authorization by $150 billion, leaving a total of $235 billion available for future buybacks.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Share repurchases and dividends\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 fiscal 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$25.78 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Approximately\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Increase in share repurchase authorization\",\n     \"period\": \"Late September 2026\",\n     \"value\": \"$150 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Total share repurchase authorization available\",\n     \"period\": \"After late September 2026 increase\",\n     \"value\": \"$235 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Available for future buybacks\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 4,\n   \"ref\": \"S37\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-26\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia estimates that its revenue growth for fiscal 2027 will be around 70%, according to Fool.com contributor Keithen Drury.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"revenue growth\",\n     \"period\": \"FY 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"around 70%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"Nvidia estimate as cited for the full fiscal year\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 9,\n   \"ref\": \"S38\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-29\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia management said demand for Vera Rubin currently implies its CPU revenue will more than double in fiscal 2028, which would position the company as one of the world's leading server CPU suppliers, according to the article.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Vera Rubin CPU revenue growth\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2028\",\n     \"value\": \"more than double\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"management statement; demand-implied\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S39\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia announced an $80 billion share buyback program at the time of its May 2026 dividend declaration, per the Morningstar article.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"share buyback program\",\n     \"period\": \"announced at the May 2026 dividend declaration\",\n     \"value\": \"$80 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"buyback authorization announced alongside the dividend increase\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 4,\n   \"ref\": \"S40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA management said Vera Rubin, its newest platform, is expected to be the fastest product ramp in the company's history, and put NVIDIA's revenue opportunity at about $40 billion per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin versus about $25 billion per gigawatt with Blackwell.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Revenue opportunity per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"$40 billion per gigawatt\",\n     \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n     \"basis\": \"Management's estimate of NVIDIA revenue opportunity per gigawatt of capacity, for Vera Rubin\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Revenue opportunity per gigawatt of capacity with Blackwell\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"$25 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n     \"basis\": \"Management's estimate of NVIDIA revenue opportunity per gigawatt of capacity, for Blackwell (comparison figure)\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S41\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-05\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's data center revenue was $89 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, up from $39 billion in the quarter of the lost H20 sales.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"data center revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q2 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$89 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"data center segment\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"data center revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"quarter of the lost H20 sales (fiscal Q1 2026)\",\n     \"value\": \"$39 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"data center segment\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S42\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-28\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia repurchased approximately $34 billion of its shares in fiscal year 2025, over $40.4 billion in fiscal year 2026, and $39 billion in the first half of fiscal year 2027 (the six months through July 2026), per the article.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"shares repurchased\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal year 2025\",\n     \"value\": \"approximately $34 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"share repurchases\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"shares repurchased\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal year 2026\",\n     \"value\": \"over $40.4 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"share repurchases\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"shares repurchased\",\n     \"period\": \"first half of fiscal year 2027 (through July 2026)\",\n     \"value\": \"$39 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"share repurchases\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 4,\n   \"ref\": \"S43\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"statement\": \"Bloomberg Intelligence forecast custom ASICs to grow at a 27% CAGR through 2033, compared with 16% for AI accelerators.\",\n   \"figures\": [],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S44\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-02\",\n   \"statement\": \"On its August 2026 earnings call, Nvidia said it returned 60% of first-half fiscal 2027 free cash flow to shareholders, ahead of its 50% target, and that going forward it intends to increase the return of free cash flow net of strategic uses.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"free cash flow returned to shareholders\",\n     \"period\": \"first half fiscal 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"60%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"share of free cash flow returned via buybacks and dividends, company statement\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"free cash flow return target\",\n     \"period\": \"first half fiscal 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"50%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"company target for share of free cash flow returned to shareholders\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S45\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-29\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's sales grew 83% in the twelve months to fiscal Q2 2027, per Trefis.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"sales growth\",\n     \"period\": \"twelve months to fiscal Q2 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"83%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"trailing twelve months\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S46\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-01\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia's revenue and profit climbed in the triple digits in its latest three-month period, to $96 billion in revenue and $59 billion in profit, according to the article, continuing the double- and triple-digit quarterly growth it says Nvidia delivered in recent years.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"latest three-month period\",\n     \"value\": \"$96 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"profit\",\n     \"period\": \"latest three-month period\",\n     \"value\": \"$59 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S47\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"statement\": \"Amazon disclosed that its Trainium business has reached multi-billion-dollar scale.\",\n   \"figures\": [],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S48\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-01\",\n   \"statement\": \"In fiscal Q2 2027, NVIDIA's hyperscale revenues increased 117% year over year to $48.71 billion, while ACIE revenues, which include AI clouds, industrial and enterprise customers, jumped 138% to $40.31 billion.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Hyperscale revenues\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 fiscal 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$48.71 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Up 117% year over year\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"ACIE revenues\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 fiscal 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$40.31 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Includes AI clouds, industrial and enterprise customers; up 138% year over year\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S49\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-25\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia's revenue rose 96% year over year to $178 billion and net income surged 161% to $118 billion in the first half of its fiscal 2027, the period ended July 26, 2026, according to the article.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"First half of fiscal 2027 (ended July 26, 2026)\",\n     \"value\": \"$178 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Company-wide revenue, up 96% year over year\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Net income\",\n     \"period\": \"First half of fiscal 2027 (ended July 26, 2026)\",\n     \"value\": \"$118 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Company-wide net income, up 161% year over year\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S50\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-26\",\n   \"statement\": \"The article states that Nvidia's data center business is still growing 117% year over year, without specifying which quarter the growth rate refers to.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"data center revenue growth, year over year\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"117%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"company's data center business; quarter not specified\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 3,\n   \"ref\": \"S51\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-27\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia's China H200 sales remain below 1% of data-center revenue, and CEO Jensen Huang has said the company's share of China's advanced AI chip market effectively fell from around 95% to zero as restrictions tightened.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"China H200 sales as share of data-center revenue\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"below 1%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Nvidia China H200 sales, share of data-center revenue\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S52\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-30\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia told investors in its prior-quarter report that it expects 70% revenue growth in its next fiscal year, citing massive AI demand, according to The Motley Fool.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"revenue growth\",\n     \"period\": \"next fiscal year (FY2028, ending late January 2028)\",\n     \"value\": \"70%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"Company revenue growth year over year, attributed by Nvidia to massive AI demand\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S53\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-29\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia's Grace CPUs, launched in 2021, generated over $5 billion in revenue over the last year, the article reports.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Grace CPU revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"last year\",\n     \"value\": \"over $5 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Grace CPUs; trailing 12 months\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S54\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-29\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia expects $20 billion in CPU sales this year, according to the article.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"CPU sales\",\n     \"period\": \"this year (calendar 2026 as described in the article)\",\n     \"value\": \"$20 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"company expectation for stand-alone CPU sales\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S55\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's gross margin came in at 75% in the last quarter, as reported by qz.com.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"gross margin\",\n     \"period\": \"last quarter\",\n     \"value\": \"75%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"company gross margin, as reported\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 11,\n   \"ref\": \"S56\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-30\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's gross margin was 75% in fiscal second-quarter 2027 and is expected to be in the 72% to 73% range for fiscal 2028, with memory costs having risen more than management expected, as reported by Fool.com.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"gross margin\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q2 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"75%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"company gross margin\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"gross margin\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2028\",\n     \"value\": \"72% to 73%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"expected range; memory costs have risen more than management expected\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S57\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"statement\": \"Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, up more than 200% year over year.\",\n   \"figures\": [],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S58\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA raised its dividend 25-fold in June and set a policy to return at least 50% of free cash flow to shareholders, according to its public June disclosures.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"dividend increase\",\n     \"period\": \"June 2026\",\n     \"value\": \"25-fold\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"free cash flow returned to shareholders\",\n     \"period\": \"Policy set in June 2026; forward-looking\",\n     \"value\": \"at least 50% of free cash flow\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"Company capital-return policy per its public June disclosures\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S59\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's days of sales outstanding, the average time to collect cash after a sale, increased to 60 days; management said this reflects extended payment terms for large purchases by certain investment-grade customers, shipped over multiple quarters.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Days of sales outstanding\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"60 days\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Average time to collect cash after a sale; management attributes the increase to extended payment terms for large purchases by certain investment-grade customers shipped over multiple quarters\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 4,\n   \"ref\": \"S60\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-30\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA's operating margin stands at 65%, a rate the article says the company has roughly maintained for the last two years.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Operating margin\",\n     \"period\": \"Last two years (roughly maintained)\",\n     \"value\": \"65%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Company operating margin; the article says the rate has been roughly maintained for the last two years\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S61\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-25\",\n   \"statement\": \"Zacks states that NVIDIA's net profit margin is 63.7%, compared with Micron's 55.9%, and that NVIDIA's return on equity of 96% exceeds Micron's 72.5%.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Net profit margin\",\n     \"period\": null,\n     \"value\": \"63.7%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"NVIDIA, compared with Micron's 55.9%\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S62\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-30\",\n   \"statement\": \"On Nvidia's Q2 earnings call, executives said the company had begun shipping a small volume of H200 accelerators to China but that these shipments amounted to less than 1 percent of its data-center revenues.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"H200 accelerator shipments to China as a share of datacenter revenues\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2\",\n     \"value\": \"less than 1 percent\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"shipments of a small volume of H200 accelerators to the region\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 2,\n   \"ref\": \"S63\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-02\",\n   \"statement\": \"Nvidia's non-GAAP EPS was $2.22 in fiscal Q2 2027, up from $1.59 in fiscal Q4 2026, a gain of about 40% in two quarters; its adjusted EPS for the latest four reported quarters was around $6.95 versus $4.64 for fiscal 2026, up about 50%. Nvidia now treats stock-based compensation as a cost in adjusted earnings and restated earlier quarters to match, according to the article.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Non-GAAP EPS\",\n     \"period\": \"Fiscal Q2 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"$2.22\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Adjusted; stock-based compensation treated as a cost\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Non-GAAP EPS\",\n     \"period\": \"Fiscal Q4 2026\",\n     \"value\": \"$1.59\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Adjusted; restated\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Non-GAAP EPS\",\n     \"period\": \"Latest four reported quarters\",\n     \"value\": \"around $6.95\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Adjusted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Non-GAAP EPS\",\n     \"period\": \"Fiscal 2026\",\n     \"value\": \"$4.64\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Adjusted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Non-GAAP EPS growth\",\n     \"period\": \"Fiscal Q4 2026 to fiscal Q2 2027\",\n     \"value\": \"around 40%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"Two quarters\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Non-GAAP EPS growth\",\n     \"period\": \"Latest four reported quarters vs fiscal 2026\",\n     \"value\": \"about 50%\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": null\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S64\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-09-22\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, a figure the article says far exceeded the 45% Wall Street had previously modeled.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Revenue growth guidance\",\n     \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028\",\n     \"value\": \"70%\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"Company guidance\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Consensus revenue growth estimate\",\n     \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028\",\n     \"value\": \"45%\",\n     \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n     \"basis\": \"Wall Street model previously expected, per the article\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 11,\n   \"ref\": \"S65\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-05\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA itself expects its volume sales to double, an expectation the MarketBeat article ties to the Vera Rubin release and to the next wave of data center construction.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Volume sales\",\n     \"period\": \"Next year\",\n     \"value\": \"double\",\n     \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n     \"basis\": \"NVIDIA's own expectation, stated as underpinned by the Vera Rubin release\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S66\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"day\": \"2026-10-05\",\n   \"statement\": \"NVIDIA returned $26.0 billion to shareholders in the quarter and had $99.0 billion remaining under its buyback authorization.\",\n   \"figures\": [\n    {\n     \"measure\": \"Buyback authorization remaining\",\n     \"period\": \"As of the report\",\n     \"value\": \"$99.0 billion\",\n     \"kind\": \"actual\",\n     \"basis\": \"remaining under buyback authorization\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"reports\": 1,\n   \"ref\": \"S67\"\n  }\n ],\n \"questions\": [\n  {\n   \"request\": \"Thesis v16 (custom-silicon, theme, focus \\\"Spending on custom AI silicon (ASICs) at cloud providers in calendar 2026\\\", 2026, due 2027-03-31): How much will cloud providers spend on custom AI silicon (ASICs) in calendar 2026?\\nLadder: rung 1 Below $40 billion: Custom-silicon spending is less than $40 billion. / rung 2 $40 billion to below $60 billion: Custom-silicon spending is at least $40 billion and less than $60 billion. / rung 3 $60 billion to below $80 billion: Custom-silicon spending is at least $60 billion and less than $80 billion. / rung 4 $80 billion to below $100 billion: Custom-silicon spending is at least $80 billion and less than $100 billion. / rung 5 $100 billion or more: Custom-silicon spending is at least $100 billion.\\n\\n[Evidence in view under this thesis, 2 items]\\n- e327 [rumour; moomoo.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September 2026.\\n    Quote: Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\\n- e502 [party_statement; Fool.com analyst, reporting Marvell’s statement; original source Marvell Technology ; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] Marvell says it has more than 50 potential custom AI chip opportunities across over 10 customers, representing potential lifetime revenue of $75 billion; no timeframe beyond “in the long run” is specified.\\n    Quote: In all, Marvell notes that it can tap into more than 50 custom AI chip opportunities across over 10 customers in the long run, leading to potential lifetime revenue of $75 billion.\\n\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]\\n- v6 (open; last_end) What share of calendar-2026 data-center AI accelerator spending will NVIDIA hold, by the first published full-year estimate?: now rung 3 Neutral; reasons: The closest market reference is the estimate that NVIDIA’s AI-chip share will be 75% in 2026, which is rung 3; longer-term estimates of 70%–75% and near 75% point to the same rung, while undated 80% estimates are less specific. The implied outcome is about 75%: those estimates concern the broader AI-chip market rather than precisely calendar-2026 data-center accelerator spending, but they are the best quantified proxies supplied. NVIDIA’s strong training position and Huawei’s low performance-adjusted share support a higher outcome; the lower inference share, growing custom-silicon alternatives\\n\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung 1; reasons: No supplied consensus, company guidance, or stated spending plan gives a market reference or a quantified 2026 spending estimate. The reported September manufacturing start is late in the year and gives no production volume or spending figure; it therefore does not imply that custom-ASIC spending reaches $40 billion. v6's neutral NVIDIA-share conclusion is consistent with custom ASICs taking some share, but does not quantify custom-ASIC spending. The most likely outcome remains below $40 billion.\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above.\",\n   \"answer\": {\n    \"rung\": 1,\n    \"implied_outcome\": \"The implied calendar-2026 spending remains below $40 billion. Marvell’s $75 billion is potential lifetime revenue across more than 50 opportunities with no specified timeframe, not 2026 spending; Meta’s reported September manufacturing start gives no production volume or spend figure, implying at most an unquantified late-year contribution. v6’s neutral NVIDIA-share conclusion is consistent with custom silicon taking some share, but does not quantify its spending.\",\n    \"reasons\": \"No quantified market consensus, company guidance, or stated 2026 spending plan is supplied, so there is no reference rung to place on the ladder. The new evidence points to some 2026 custom-silicon activity, but neither item quantifies calendar-2026 provider spending; the implied outcome remains below $40 billion rather than crossing the $40 billion boundary.\"\n   },\n   \"ref\": \"Q13\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"ref\": \"Q4\",\n   \"request\": \"Thesis v4 (NVDA, asset, focus \\\"Whether Vera Rubin moves from full production to volume customer shipments and first revenue recognition within NVIDIA's fiscal 2027, as shown in the company's quarterly results and Form 10-K.\\\", 2027, due 2027-01-31): Will NVIDIA recognize revenue from Vera Rubin volume customer shipments by the end of FY2027, as disclosed in its quarterly results or FY2027 Form 10-K?\\nLadder: rung 1 Yes: NVIDIA's quarterly results or FY2027 Form 10-K disclose that it has begun recognizing revenue from Vera Rubin volume customer shipments by 2027-01-31. / rung 2 Ruled out: After 2026-09-23 and before 2027-01-31, NVIDIA formally abandons or cancels the Vera Rubin platform. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-09-23 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not. / rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\\n\\n[Evidence in view under this thesis, 53 items]\\n[Not shown: 37 more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]\\n- e85 [party_statement; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:44b5d56e3c6718335d33ab2b 2026-09-23] NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin platform has entered the full production stage, positioning the company to benefit from the next phase of AI infrastructure investment, as reported by Zacks.\\n    Quote: Additionally, the next-generation Vera Rubin platform has entered the full production stage, positioning NVIDIA to benefit from the next phase of AI infrastructure investment.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e90, e185, e251, e283, e291, e320, e343; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e89 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nebius Group; CoreWeave ; from gnews:a5837f6a8cb2c7893ec87974 2026-09-23] Nebius Group announced another increase in prices for NVIDIA GPU rentals, and CoreWeave said it was continuing to contract new compute capacity at higher prices; the article cites both as fresh evidence that demand for NVIDIA-powered computing remains strong. No price levels, capacity amounts or dates are given.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, demand from AI cloud providers remains robust as Nebius Group (NBIS) announced another increase in prices for Nvidia GPU rentals, while CoreWeave (CRWV) said it was continuing to contract new compute capacity at higher prices, providing fresh evidence that demand for Nvidia-powered computing remains strong.\\n- e90 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA management 2026-08-26; from gnews:a5837f6a8cb2c7893ec87974 2026-09-23] NVIDIA management pointed to full production of its next-generation Vera Rubin AI platform, and the article says continued AI infrastructure strength is accelerating NVIDIA's AI growth trajectory. The statement does not say Vera Rubin has begun volume customer shipments or revenue recognition.\\n    Quote: It's worth noting that Nvidia is not merely maintaining its AI growth trajectory; it is accelerating it, with management pointing to full production of its next-generation Vera Rubin platform and continued strength across AI infrastructure.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e85; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e181 [fact; GuruFocus (gurufocus.com); original source Super Micro Computer 2026-09-24; from gnews:cd0056006ad115260ae2b646 2026-09-24] Super Micro Computer moved into commercial shipments of servers built around NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin platform, shipping Vera Rubin NVL72 racks through its Data Center Building Block Solutions that combine computing hardware with liquid cooling, networking, storage and power components; each rack design uses 72 Rubin GPUs and 36 Vera CPUs, according to a GuruFocus report published 24 September 2026.\\n    Quote: the server maker moved into commercial shipments of systems built around NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin platform, adding another data-center product to its AI infrastructure lineup. … The company is shipping Vera Rubin NVL72 racks through its Data Center Building Block Solutions, combining computing hardware with liquid cooling, networking, storage and power components. The rack design uses 7\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e859, e951; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e188 [party_statement; fool.com (article via Yahoo Finance); original source SpaceX (Elon Musk, CEO) ; from gnews:943a57daed49d866fe468605 2026-09-24] On SpaceX's second-quarter earnings call, SpaceX CEO Elon Musk said SpaceX has decided to build exclusively on NVIDIA hardware because he considers the Vera Rubin architecture the best architecture and the best AI computer, citing close cooperation and partnership with NVIDIA; the article characterises this as making SpaceX (which owns xAI and its Grok model) exclusive to NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: During SpaceX's second-quarter earnings call, Musk had this to say about SpaceX's relationship with Nvidia: … We've decided to build exclusively on NVIDIA because we think the Vera Rubin architecture is the best architecture. We think it's the best AI computer, and we greatly value our close cooperation and partnership on many levels with NVIDIA. So, we're exclusive to NVIDIA.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e387, e396; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e208 [fact; Zacks (zacks.com); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7fb0b2b7d22b8bb07625b212 2026-09-24] NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin platform began production shipments in the third quarter, according to Zacks; the item gives no volume, customer or revenue-recognition figure for the shipments.\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin began production shipments in the third quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e234, e409, e598, e650, e721, e857; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e234 [fact; Trefis; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:06218d9421731e5e59c1dbef 2026-09-24] NVIDIA began production shipments of its Vera Rubin platform in August, with purchase orders already received from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud and system OEM, according to a 24 September 2026 article.\\n    Quote: Production shipments began in August, with purchase orders already in from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud, and system OEM.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e208; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e236 [party_statement; Trefis; original source NVIDIA (CFO) ; from gnews:06218d9421731e5e59c1dbef 2026-09-24] NVIDIA's CFO expects supply to remain a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028 and calls memory pricing extreme; the article reports memory prices have risen more than management expected.\\n    Quote: The CFO expects supply to stay a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028 and calls memory pricing extreme. … Memory prices have risen more than management expected, and the guide has that margin settling in the 72% to 73% range in fiscal 2028, helped by price increases NVIDIA has already executed.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e271, e413, e414, e556, e653, e774, e864, e865; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e243 [fact; Kieron Allen, Cloud Wars (cloudwars.com); original source Amazon Web Services and NVIDIA (joint announcement) ; from gnews:7c4283c55cf02ba9cfd9a835 2026-09-24] Amazon Web Services and NVIDIA announced an expansion of their long-standing partnership under which AWS will deploy 2 million additional NVIDIA GPUs across its infrastructure between 2027 and 2028, spanning NVIDIA's Blackwell Ultra, Rubin and Rubin Ultra architectures and deployed alongside NVIDIA Vera CPUs; the addition builds on the more than 1 million NVIDIA GPUs AWS had previously committed to deploying beginning in 2026, and Amazon said the aim is to meet surging demand for AI infrastructure from frontier labs, global enterprises, start-ups and governments. The number of GPUs is a planned deployment, not reported deliveries or revenue.\\n    Quote: Now, the two powerhouses have announced a staggering expansion of this existing partnership which will, among other things — but this is certainly the standout headline — include the deployment of 2 million additional NVIDIA GPUs across AWS infrastructure between 2027 and 2028. … The aim, according to Amazon, is to meet surging demand for AI infrastructure “from frontier labs, global enterprises, \\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e279 [third_party_view; qz.com, citing MarketWatch; original source Mehdi Hosseini, Susquehanna analyst (remarks to MarketWatch) ; from gnews:460160402f7a10882d1e925f 2026-09-25] Susquehanna analyst Mehdi Hosseini, in remarks reported by MarketWatch and cited by qz.com, said Micron's November-quarter (fiscal Q1 2026) sales forecast is strong enough to satisfy investors but will not fully reflect the benefits of the Nvidia product ramp; he said some estimated revenue is expected to shift toward next year instead of this year, implying the Nvidia-chip-related revenue payoff may be delayed.\\n    Quote: Micron $MU Technology posted record fiscal fourth-quarter revenue and issued strong guidance for the current quarter, but one analyst says investors may need to wait longer to see the full payoff from an Nvidia $NVDA chip launch. … Susquehanna analyst Mehdi Hosseini told MarketWatch that Micron 's November-quarter sales forecast looks strong enough to satisfy investors, though it won't fully refle\\n- e283 [party_statement; MarketBeat; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:91b917994e36036e304616e8 2026-09-25] NVIDIA states that its Vera Rubin AI platform is already in full production, with production shipments beginning in August 2026 and purchase orders received from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud and system original equipment manufacturer (OEM), as reported by MarketBeat.\\n    Quote: The trigger for this move could come from subsequent earnings reports and continued progress with Vera Rubin. The platform is already in full production, with NVIDIA reporting production shipments beginning in August and purchase orders from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud and system original equipment manufacturer (OEM).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e85; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e370 [fact; cryptorank.io; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:844106b7a25ecc1175290290 2026-09-26] Nvidia reported that in the latest MLPerf Inference v6.1 tests its next-generation Vera Rubin NVL72 delivered up to 3.7x the throughput of its GB300 NVL72 on the Qwen3-VL benchmark and up to 2.5x on DeepSeek-R1, and described the Vera Rubin entry in its official MLPerf announcement as a preview submission ahead of broader deployment.\\n    Quote: In the latest MLPerf Inference v6.1 tests, Vera Rubin NVL72 delivered up to 3.7x the throughput of Nvidia’s GB300 NVL72 on the Qwen3-VL benchmark. On DeepSeek-R1, the improvement reached as much as 2.5x. … Nvidia detailed the results in its official MLPerf announcement , describing Vera Rubin’s entry as a preview submission ahead of broader deployment.\\n- e409 [fact; Trefis; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d4f3bddf04a4d029a097541c 2026-09-27] NVIDIA began production shipments of its newest data center system, Vera Rubin, in August 2026, according to the article.